(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase467ToolReliabilityAndScenarioCoverage"
  :createdAt 1789291000000
  :status "planned"
  :priorityOrder 3
  :summary "Tool Reliability and Scenario Coverage: an inventory an agent can see, a scenario matrix per tool, a stated engine and process model, and the search and dependency surfaces measured rather than assumed."
  :phase "Phase467ToolReliabilityAndScenarioCoverage"
  :baseline "Probed 2026-09-12. Of ten declared rpc operations eight answer the question asked: :sym, :out, :read, :ls, :sec, :find, and :callers and :impact which returned 29 and 30 results for a real symbol, so dependency comprehension exists and works. Two do not: :grep and :q both dispatch to the find handler and return :status ok, :grep answering a request for one symbol under one directory with 320 files matching a default glob. Separately the CLI surface that documents this capability is absent: asl intel, asl doc, asl task and asl doctor do not exist, so the working :callers and :impact are reachable only through rpc and are named nowhere an agent reads. No tool has a scenario suite. The engine is a C host embedding a JavaScript evaluator on JavaScriptCore, macOS only, and where it runs and how it manages processes is stated nowhere."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task46701" :parentId "" :phase "phase-467"
      :title "An inventory the agent can see, with measured status per tool"
      :kind :tooling :state :planned :lane "inventory" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789291000000 :updatedAt 1789291000000
      :motivation "An agent cannot choose well among tools it cannot enumerate. Today the enumeration is spread across a rule that lists rpc ops with warnings, a capability registry whose 36 statuses are hand written, and two instruction files naming eleven commands that do not exist. The working :callers and :impact are named in no surface at all, so the one capability that answers how everything connects is the one nobody is told about."
      :purpose "One inventory lists every tool and operation with what it does, what it returns, its measured status and its named fallback, generated from the probe results rather than written by hand, and rendered into the agent surface at the tier where affordances belong."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["One generated inventory with measured status" "Working operations discoverable" "Fallback named per degraded operation" "Rendered at the affordance tier"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/capabilities.asn" "asl/tools/asl.c" "scripts/install.sh"]
      :targetSymbols ["capabilities"] :relatedSymbols ["capabilities" "tools" "ssot"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46403" "Task46602"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46701"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46701.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Breaking a tool changes its inventory status with no hand edit." "A tool absent from the inventory but reachable is reported." "Every degraded entry names a fallback that itself measures as working."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46701" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Generate from probes." "Render at the affordance tier." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task46702" :parentId "" :phase "phase-467"
      :title "A scenario matrix per tool, not a happy path per tool"
      :kind :verification :state :planned :lane "coverage" :priority :critical :ownerRole "verifier"
      :createdAt 1789291000000 :updatedAt 1789291000000
      :motivation "The defect that let :grep answer a different question for months is exactly the defect a happy path test cannot find, because :grep returns a plausible list. Tools fail on the edges: an empty file, a file that is not there, a path that escapes the root, a name with a space or a non Latin character, a symlink, a file too large to hold, a binary, a concurrent writer, a path at the length limit. None of these has a case anywhere."
      :purpose "Every tool carries a matrix of scenarios rather than an example: absent, empty, large, binary, unicode, symlinked, permission denied, concurrently modified, path traversal, and the normal case last. Each scenario asserts on the result and on the failure mode, so a tool that degrades silently under one of them is caught by the scenario that produces it."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["A scenario matrix per tool" "Assertions on failure mode, not only on success" "Silent degradation caught by the scenario that causes it" "The matrix reused for every base language"]
      :owns ["tests/probes" "docs/EXAMPLE_DOCTRINE.md"]
      :targetSymbols [] :relatedSymbols ["gates" "capabilities" "bounded"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46406"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46702"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46702.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A path escaping the workspace root is refused and the refusal names the path." "A tool returning a plausible wrong answer fails its scenario rather than passing on shape." "A tool with fewer scenarios than the matrix requires is reported as uncovered."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46702" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Define the matrix." "Instantiate per tool." "Report uncovered tools." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task46703" :parentId "" :phase "phase-467"
      :title "Content search and process handling become first class and measured"
      :kind :engine :state :planned :lane "coverage" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789291000000 :updatedAt 1789291000000
      :motivation "Content search is the operation an agent reaches for most and it is the one that lies. Process handling has no declared surface at all, so anything long running is spawned without a stated model for its lifetime, its output or its failure. Both are the places where an agent burns a turn and learns nothing."
      :purpose "Content search returns matches with path, line and the matched span, bounded and continuable, and fails explicitly rather than degrading into a filename search. Process handling declares how a process is started, how its output is bounded, how it is ended and what happens when it outlives the session. Both are probed by the scenario matrix."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Content search returns spans and never degrades to filenames" "A declared process model with bounded output and a stated lifetime" "Both covered by the scenario matrix"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "asl/grammar/rpc.asn" "asl/packages/asl-sh/src"]
      :targetSymbols ["rpc"] :relatedSymbols ["tools" "bounded" "capabilities"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46402" "Task46702"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46703"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46703.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A search for a string present in one file returns that file, that line and that span, and nothing else." "A search with no matches returns an empty result rather than a filename list." "A process producing unbounded output is truncated at a stated bound and says it was truncated."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46703" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Implement search properly." "Declare the process model." "Cover both by matrix." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task46704" :parentId "" :phase "phase-467"
      :title "How everything connects, as a queryable surface"
      :kind :tooling :state :planned :lane "graph" :priority :high :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789291000000 :updatedAt 1789291000000
      :motivation "The capability an agent most needs for an unfamiliar codebase is what depends on what, and it already exists: :callers and :impact returned 29 and 30 results for a real symbol. It is named in no instruction surface, has no CLI, and is not connected to the module index the resolver work is building, so the same graph is about to be computed twice and disagree."
      :purpose "One graph answers definition, callers, dependents and blast radius, built from the same module index the evaluator binds against, so the analyser and the runtime cannot diverge. It is bounded and continuable, it names the base language of each node, and it is discoverable from the inventory."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["One graph shared by evaluator and analysers" "Callers, dependents and blast radius from it" "Bounded and continuable" "Discoverable from the inventory"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "intel/src" "asl/grammar/rpc.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["callers" "impact" "resolveModulePath"] :relatedSymbols ["tools" "context" "bounded"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task45701" "Task46701"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46704"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46704.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Adding a call adds an edge visible to both the graph query and the evaluator." "Blast radius for a symbol includes every module that transitively binds it and nothing else." "The graph and the resolver disagree on no edge, checked by comparing them."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46704" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Share the index." "Expose the queries." "Compare against the resolver." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task46705" :parentId "" :phase "phase-467"
      :title "Where the engine runs, and what that costs the tooling"
      :kind :architecture :state :planned :lane "engine" :priority :high :ownerRole "planner"
      :createdAt 1789291000000 :updatedAt 1789291000000
      :motivation "The tooling behaves differently depending on where the engine is, and where it is has never been written down. Module resolution currently depends on the process working directory, so the same command answers differently from two directories. The engine is macOS only, and the relay work assumes a browser runtime that cannot exist while the language and the engine are one artefact."
      :purpose "The engine model is stated: what a session is, where the root is determined from, whether state persists between invocations, and what the tooling may assume. Anything that varies with the working directory either stops varying or declares that it does. The model is the same document the host interface work is built against, so one answer serves both."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["A stated engine and session model" "Working directory dependence removed or declared" "One model shared with the host interface work" "Browser and mobile targets answerable"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/protocol-conformance.asn" "asl/tools/asl.c" ".asl.config.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["discovered_ws" "run_evaluator"] :relatedSymbols ["foreign" "capabilities"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D34" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46103"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46705"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46705.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["The same command run from two directories gives the same answer, or declares the dependence." "A session assumption not in the model is contradicted by a test." "The model answers where a browser target obtains its root."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46705" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["State the model." "Remove or declare directory dependence." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task46706" :parentId "" :phase "phase-467"
      :title "ASL first, other base languages by the same matrix"
      :kind :tooling :state :planned :lane "coverage" :priority :moderate :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789291000000 :updatedAt 1789291000000
      :motivation "The tools are used against whatever the repository holds, and a tool correct on ASL and wrong on another language fails silently in exactly the way :grep did. Coverage stated for one language and assumed for the rest is how that happens."
      :purpose "Each tool declares the base languages it supports, and the scenario matrix runs per declared language. A language not declared is refused rather than attempted, so the failure is a refusal and not a wrong answer."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Declared language support per tool" "The matrix run per language" "An undeclared language refused rather than mishandled"]
      :owns ["tests/probes" "asl/grammar/capabilities.asn" "intel/src"]
      :targetSymbols [] :relatedSymbols ["capabilities" "foreign"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46702" "Task46704"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46706"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46706.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["An undeclared language produces a refusal naming the language." "A declared language passes the full matrix." "Adding a language requires running the matrix, not editing a claim."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46706" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Declare support per tool." "Run the matrix per language." "Refuse the undeclared." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])]
  :notes "Eight of ten operations already answer correctly, including the dependency comprehension the owner asks about. The work is not to build tools but to make the working ones visible, the lying ones fail, and every one of them survive a scenario that is not the happy path.")
